    "category": "mobility",
    "ageGroup": "8-11",
    "glossary": {
      "90/90 Hip Switches": "Sit with both knees bent at 90 degrees, one in front and one to the side, rotate to switch which leg is in front without using hands.",
      "Ankle Circles": "Lift one foot slightly off the ground and rotate at the ankle, making slow full circles each direction.",
      "Arm Circles": "Extend arms straight out to the sides and make slow, controlled circles, increasing size gradually.",
      "Deep Squat Hold": "Sit down into the bottom of a squat as low as comfortable, chest up, hold the position and relax into it.",
      "Fielding-Position Hip Openers": "From an athletic fielding stance, rotate one knee outward and back like opening a gate, alternate sides.",
      "Forward Fold": "Stand tall, slowly hinge forward reaching toward the toes, keep a slight bend in the knees, let the back relax.",
      "Full Body Flow": "Move through the program's earlier stretches back to back as one connected sequence, no rest between movements.",
      "Shoulder Cross-Body Stretch": "Bring one arm straight across the chest, use the other arm to gently pull it closer, feel the stretch in the shoulder.",
      "Standing Bat-Swing Rotation": "Stand in an athletic stance and slowly rotate the torso through a swing-like motion without a bat, focus on full rotation.",
      "Standing Quad Stretch": "Stand on one leg, grab the opposite ankle behind you, gently pull the heel toward the glutes while keeping knees together.",
      "Throwing Arm Circles": "With throwing arm extended, make slow controlled circles forward and backward to loosen the shoulder.",
      "Throwing Shoulder Sleeper Stretch": "Lie on the throwing-arm side, bend that elbow to 90 degrees, gently press the forearm down toward the ground with the other hand.",
      "Torso Twists": "Stand with feet planted, rotate the upper body side to side with control, let the arms swing naturally.",
      "Walking Forward Fold": "Take a step forward then fold forward reaching toward the ground, alternate which foot leads each step.",
      "Walking Quad Stretch": "Take a step, then grab the trailing foot and pull the heel toward the glutes briefly before stepping again.",
      "World's Greatest Stretch": "Step into a deep lunge, place both hands inside the front foot, rotate the torso and reach one arm toward the ceiling, then switch sides."
    },
