    "glossary": {
      "3-Cone L-Drill (timed)": "Set 3 cones in an L shape 5 yards apart, sprint to the first, back to start, around the outside of all 3 and back through start as fast as possible.",
      "5-10-5 Pro Agility (timed)": "Start in the middle of 3 cones 5 yards apart, sprint 5 yards and touch, 10 yards opposite and touch, 5 yards back through start.",
      "A-Skips": "Skip forward driving the knee sharply up to hip height, push off the toes powerfully, pump the opposite arm.",
      "Acceleration Sprint (3-point stance)": "Set up in a 3-point stance, explode forward on signal, drive forward aggressively for the distance given.",
      "Ankling Drill": "Walk forward with very quick light toe-to-ball-to-toe contacts, ankle stiffness is the key, keep ground contact minimal.",
      "B-Skips": "Like A-Skips but actively claw the leg back down toward the ground before pushing off.",
      "Banded Hip Drive Sprint": "Attach a band around the hips to a fixed point behind you, drive forward against the resistance focusing on hip extension.",
      "Box Drill (reactive)": "4-cone box, coach calls a direction or color as athlete moves, athlete reacts and changes path mid-movement.",
      "Broad Jump": "Swing arms and jump forward as far as possible off both feet, land softly on both feet.",
      "Flying 30": "Build speed gradually over 20 yards then hit absolute maximum velocity for the final 30 yards.",
      "Hurdle Hops (single-leg)": "Hop over low hurdles on one leg, land softly, minimize ground contact time, switch legs each set.",
      "Mirror Drill (competitive)": "Face a partner, one leads with direction changes, the other mirrors reactively, compete to maintain position.",
      "Overspeed Sprint (band-assisted)": "Attach a light band to the waist with a partner providing light forward pull, run faster than normal top speed.",
      "Power Skip": "Exaggerate the A-Skip with maximum height and distance, drive the knee as high as possible.",
      "Reactive Cone Sprint": "Multiple cones in various directions, coach calls a cone number or color and athlete sprints to it immediately.",
      "Resisted Sprint": "Resistance band attached to the waist, partner holds the other end, sprint hard against the resistance.",
      "Sled Push": "Low athletic stance, drive the sled forward with short powerful steps, lean into it, drive through the balls of the feet.",
      "Wall Drill (double-leg)": "Both hands on a wall, drive both knees up alternately in a quick rhythm, practice the sprint cycle mechanics."
    },
