    "category": "mobility",
    "ageGroup": "16-18",
    "glossary": {
      "90/90 Hip Internal Rotation": "Sit in 90/90 position, gently press the front knee toward the ground to increase internal rotation of the hip.",
      "Active Leg Lowering": "Lie on your back, raise one leg straight up, slowly lower it toward the ground while keeping the other leg flat, stop before the lower back arches.",
      "Ankle Dorsiflexion Stretch": "In a lunge position, drive the front knee forward over the toes as far as possible without the heel leaving the ground.",
      "Cat-Cow": "On hands and knees, arch the back up (cat) then drop the belly and lift the head (cow), slow and controlled breathing throughout.",
      "Couch Stretch": "Place one knee near a wall, raise that foot up the wall, drive the hip forward while keeping the torso upright.",
      "Cross-Body Shoulder Stretch": "Bring one arm straight across the chest, use the other arm to pull it closer, feel the rear shoulder and rotator cuff.",
      "Dead Hang": "Hang from a pull-up bar with full grip, let the shoulders fully decompress and the spine lengthen, breathe and relax.",
      "Deep Squat to Stand": "Hold a deep squat position with arms extended, then stand fully and repeat, works hips, ankles, and thoracic spine together.",
      "Half-Kneeling Hip Flexor Stretch": "Kneel on one knee, squeeze the glute of the kneeling leg, push the hip forward until you feel the front of the hip stretch.",
      "Hip 90/90 Flow": "From 90/90, rotate slowly through both hip positions back and forth without using hands, controlled and smooth.",
      "Kneeling Thoracic Rotation with Reach": "Half-kneeling position, one hand behind head, rotate the elbow as high toward the ceiling as possible, follow with the eyes.",
      "Lat Stretch (overhead bar)": "Grip a rack or bar overhead with one hand, step back slightly, push the hip away and let the lat fully stretch.",
      "Pigeon Pose": "From push-up position, bring one knee forward behind the wrist, extend the other leg back, square the hips and hold.",
      "Posterior Shoulder Capsule Stretch": "Lie on the throwing-arm side, bend elbow to 90 degrees, use the other hand to gently press the forearm toward the ground.",
      "Prone Press-Up": "Lie face down, place hands near the shoulders, press the chest up while keeping the hips on the ground, like an upward dog.",
      "Scorpion Stretch": "Lie face down, swing one foot up and across the body toward the opposite hand while keeping the shoulders flat on the ground.",
      "Seated Hamstring Stretch": "Sit with legs straight, hinge forward from the hips with a flat back reaching toward the toes.",
      "Side-Lying Thoracic Rotation": "Lie on your side with knees stacked at 90 degrees, reach the top arm across and rotate the thoracic spine, follow the arm with your eyes.",
      "Standing Hip CARs": "Stand on one leg, draw the largest possible circle with the opposite knee, moving slowly through every degree of hip range.",
      "Thoracic Foam Roll": "Place a foam roller under the mid-back horizontally, support the head, gently extend over it at different segments.",
      "World's Greatest Stretch": "Deep lunge position, both hands inside the front foot, rotate one arm toward the ceiling, hold at the top before switching."
    },
